<h1>Juliana Stratton</h1>
<p>United States Senate, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Democratic.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.julianastratton.com" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (julianastratton.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Won the March primary over Raja Krishnamoorthi and Robin Kelly and says she is running to put middle-class families at the center of federal policy. Her campaign opposes the Trump administration&#39;s tariffs, immigration enforcement tactics, and cuts to healthcare and food assistance, and cites her seven years as lieutenant governor as preparation for the seat.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Lieutenant governor of Illinois since 2019; previously a state representative, justice-policy director at UIC and Cook County, and longtime president of a mediation firm.</p>
